    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d817">

                <pb facs="0866" n="852" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg852"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.733/163: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Colombia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Daniels</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-05-27T12:00:00-05:00">May 27,
                            1944—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received May 28—2:55 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>965. For De Wolf<anchor n="19" xml:id="d817-f1"/> from Otterman.<anchor n="20"
                        xml:id="d817-f2"/> Minister Posts and Telegraphs<anchor n="21"
                        xml:id="d817-f3"/> and our delegation have arrived at complete agreement
                    more satisfactory than our telegram May 23.<anchor n="22" xml:id="d817-f4"/> It
                    will be confirmed by exchange of notes between Embassy and Colombian Foreign
                        Minister<anchor n="23" xml:id="d817-f5"/> probably Monday.<anchor n="24"
                        xml:id="d817-f6"/> Embassy will advise when notes signed. Text of note
                    follows:</p>
                <p>[Here follows text of note to be exchanged with Colombian Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs, not printed.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed> [Otterman] <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Daniels</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d817-f1" n="19" xml:id="d817-f1-content">
                <p>Francis C. de Wolf, Chief, Telecommunications Division.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d817-f2" n="20" xml:id="d817-f2-content">
                <p>Harvey B. Otterman, Assistant Chief, Telecommunications Division.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d817-f3" n="21" xml:id="d817-f3-content">
                <p>Alirio Gómez Picón.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d817-f4" n="22" xml:id="d817-f4-content">
                <p>Telegram 935, not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d817-f5" n="23" xml:id="d817-f5-content">
                <p>Carlos Lozano y Lozano.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d817-f6" n="24" xml:id="d817-f6-content">
                <p>The agreement was signed on May 31, 1944, but was not put into effect; see third
                    paragraph of despatch 4426, September 13, from Bogotá, <ref target="#pg860">p.
                        860</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
